=========================================================================
🚀 MODULE 2: TEXT ARCHITECTURE & TYPOGRAPHY (HEADING, PARAGRAPH & SEMANTIC)
=========================================================================
Description: Browser website ke text ko kaise read aur rank karta hai, semantic 
importance (Meaning) aur visual styles ke beech ka asli farq kya hai.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. HEADINGS (<h1> to <h6>) - Hierarchy aur Importance
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HTML mein total 6 type ki headings hoti hain. Inka kaam sirf text ka size 
bada-chota karna nahi, balki code ki hierarchy (importance) batana hota hai:

* <h1> (The King Tag): Yeh sabse badi aur sabse important heading hoti hai. 
  Pure HTML page par koshish karke SURF EK HI <h1> tag hona chahiye. Google 
  ka Search Engine crawler sabse pehle aapke <h1> ko hi padhta hai taaki 
  wo samajh sake ki page kis main topic par bana hai.
* <h6> (The Smallest): Yeh hierarchy mein sabse choti aur sabse kam 
  important heading hoti hai.

⚠️ INTERVIEW WARNING / COMMON MISTAKE:
Naye developers aksar kisi normal text ko bada dikhane ke liye bina soche 
<h1> ya <h2> use kar lete hain. Yeh bilkul galat practice hai! Text ka size 
bada ya chota karna CSS (Layout styling) ka kaam hai. HTML tags ka kaam sirf 
browser aur Google ko text ka "Matlab" (Importance) batana hai.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. STRUCTURAL TAGS (Dhaancha Khada Karne Wale Tags)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
* <p> (Paragraph Tag):
  Yeh text ko ek block mein break karta hai. Jab aap <p> use karte ho, toh 
  browser automatically paragraph ke upar aur niche thodi khali jagah 
  (default margin) chodh deta hai.

* <br> (Line Break):
  Yeh ek Empty tag ya Self-Closing tag hai (yaani iska koi aakhri closing 
  companion </br> nahi hota). Yeh chalte huye text ko wahi rok kar turant 
  agli nayi line par bhej deta hai, bina paragraph badle.

* <hr> (Horizontal Rule):
  Yeh bhi ek self-closing tag hai. Yeh pure page par ek patli si horizontal 
  line (laker) khinch deta hai. Iska use tab kiya jata hai jab aapko website 
  par koi bada topic ya section change karna ho.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. SEMANTIC EMPHASIS (Visual Style vs Asli Meaning)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aksar log sochte hain ki <b> aur <strong> dono ka kaam text ko bold karna hai, 
aur <i> aur <em> dono ka kaam italic karna hai. Par search engines aur screen 
readers ke liye dono ka matlab bilkul alag hai:

* <b> (Bold Style) vs <strong> (Semantic Importance)
  - <b>: Yeh sirf text ko aankhon ke liye mota (visual style) karta hai. 
    Browser ke liye iska koi special ya important matlab nahi hota.
  - <strong>: Yeh text ko physically bold bhi karta hai aur sath hi Google 
    + Browser ko bolta hai ki: "Bhai, yeh text pure page mein sabse zaroori 
    hissa hai." Jo blind log screen reader use karte hain, unka software 
    <strong> waale text ko thoda zor dekar (loudly) padhta hai.

* <i> (Italic Style) vs <em> (Emphasis)
  - <i>: Yeh text ko sirf design ya style dene ke liye tedha (italic) karta hai.
  - <em>: Yeh browser ko batata hai ki is specific shabd par stress (zor) dena 
    hai, jisse sentence ka tone badal jata hai.

🛠️ LIVE CODE EXAMPLE FOR NOTES:
<p>Humaara mission hai <strong>HTML5 mein expert</strong> banna.</p>
<!-- Yahan 'HTML5 mein expert' par sabse zyada zor diya gaya hai -->

<p>Is kitab ke lekhak ka naam <i>Rahul Sharma</i> hai.</p>
<!-- Yahan 'Rahul Sharma' ko sirf ek unique name style dene ke liye italic kiya hai -->

=========================================================================
